  "extraction_notes": "Figure shows a generic DATB-catalyzed amidation scope plus products 17–28. Catalyst 8a (DATB) structure is not drawn in this panel, so its SMILES is left empty. Several precursor acid structures (10a, 10c–10m) are referenced only by labels and are not explicitly drawn here; product structures were extracted directly from the drawings, while precursor acid names/structures are inferred only where obvious. Product 23 appears to be an anisamide/benzylamide from the drawing, but the exact dimethoxy substitution pattern on acid 10h is not fully certain from the low-resolution image. Product 27 heteroaryl acyl fragment is low-confidence due to indistinct ring labeling; encoded as a fused bicyclic aromatic carboxamide matching the visible skeleton but flagged for review. Product 21 bicyclic acid fragment and product 26 quinolinecarboxamide regiochemistry were inferred from the product drawings and should be human-checked."
}